NAME
    dupes - detect duplicated code overlapping recent changes

SYNOPSIS
    dupes [--base <rev>] [--min-tokens N] [--warn-tokens N]
          [--lang cs|rust|all] [--repo <dir>]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.dev module (linked into standalone dianash(1)).
    Runs PMD's copy-paste detector (CPD) across tracked .rs and .cs files
    in the repository and prints each duplicated block on one line:

        file:first-last  duplicates  file:first-last  (N tokens)

    With --base <rev>, only blocks overlapping lines added in
    'git diff -U0 <rev>..HEAD' are reported, with the newly added range
    listed first. A range is treated as a new copy when added lines cover
    at least half of it; a range merely touched by an edit prints as
    'warning: touches an existing duplicate: <line>' and does not fail
    the run. Without --base, the entire repository is audited, ranked by
    tokens times occurrences.

    dupes reads the repository directly on the host filesystem rather
    than through the DianaSh sandbox. Two optional repository-root files
    control filtering:

    dupes.ignore    One path pattern per line ('#' starts a comment),
                    matched against consecutive path segments ('*'
                    matches within a segment), to exclude generated
                    tables, tests, examples, benches, build output, and
                    reference trees.
    dupes.accept    Accepted duplicates, one per line: the two ranges
                    formatted as dupes prints them, two spaces, and a
                    required reason. Accepted pairs are skipped while
                    both line ranges remain unchanged.

    Because CPD inspects working-tree files while --base reads committed
    diffs, run dupes on a clean committed tree for accurate line ranges.
    Summary statistics are written to standard error.

OPTIONS
    --base <rev>
        Limit reporting to duplicates overlapping lines added since
        <rev>..HEAD.
    --min-tokens N
        Minimum token count that fails the run (default: 100).
    --warn-tokens N
        Minimum token count passed to CPD (default: 75). Findings from
        --warn-tokens up to --min-tokens - 1 print with a 'warning: '
        prefix and do not fail the run. Must not exceed --min-tokens.
    --lang cs|rust|all
        Restrict scanning to C# (.cs, with CPD --ignore-usings), Rust
        (.rs), or both (default: all).
    --repo <dir>
        Path to the git repository (overrides EMUSEN_REPO and current
        working directory).

ENVIRONMENT
    EMUSEN_CPD      Path to the PMD executable (default:
                    ~/.cache/emusen/toolchains/pmd-7.28.0/bin/pmd).
    EMUSEN_REPO     Repository root when --repo is not given.

EXAMPLES
    EMUSEN_REPO=$PWD dianash -c 'dupes --base HEAD~1'
    EMUSEN_REPO=$PWD dianash -c 'dupes --lang rust --min-tokens 150'

EXIT STATUS
    0   No findings at or above --min-tokens.
    1   One or more findings at or above --min-tokens.
    2   Execution error (PMD missing, git error, invalid option, or
        malformed dupes.accept).

SEE ALSO
    hwcount(1), qml-rules(1), esde-check(1), theme-check(1)
